@startuml crc
' Source: docs/design/requirements.md, section "CRC Analysis"
' CRC cards only: no relationship arrows between cards.
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide circle

class CurrencyPair {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Know its name (for example, EUR_USD)
  Know its past price data
  Know its current market structure
  .. Collaborators ..
}

class TradeSetup {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Know which currency pair it belongs to
  Know its direction, entry price, stop loss, and take profit
  (direction comes from BuySetup or SellSetup)
  Know its reward-to-risk ratio
  Know its outcome (win, loss, or open) on its pair's price data
  (FR3; computed by BuySetup or SellSetup)
  .. Collaborators ..
  CurrencyPair
}

class BuySetup {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Know that its direction is buy
  Require stop loss < entry < take profit
  Know its reward (take profit − entry) and its risk (entry − stop loss)
  Know its outcome: a win when a high reaches take profit,
  a loss when a low reaches stop loss
  .. Collaborators ..
}

class SellSetup {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Know that its direction is sell
  Require take profit < entry < stop loss
  Know its reward (entry − take profit) and its risk (stop loss − entry)
  Know its outcome: a win when a low reaches take profit,
  a loss when a high reaches stop loss
  .. Collaborators ..
}

class BacktestResult {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Know which currency pair was tested
  Know which trade setups were tested
  Know its number of trades and its win rate
  Know when the test was run
  Know the number of wins
  .. Collaborators ..
  CurrencyPair
  TradeSetup (Phase 06)
}

class Candle {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Know its currency pair and timeframe
  Know its time, open, high, low, close, and volume
  Reject an incomplete candle, a high below its low,
  an open or close outside [low, high], and any price <= 0 (FR6)
  .. Collaborators ..
  CurrencyPair
  Timeframe
}

class SwingPoint {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Know its currency pair and timeframe
  Know its time, its price, and whether it is a high or a low
  Know its label: HH or LH for a high, HL or LL for a low (FR7)
  .. Collaborators ..
  CurrencyPair
  Timeframe
}

class StructureEvent {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Know the swing point it broke
  Know the time and the close price of the break
  Know its direction, bullish or bearish
  (kind comes from BreakOfStructure or ChangeOfCharacter)
  Require the close to be beyond the swing point's price in its direction
  .. Collaborators ..
  SwingPoint
}

class BreakOfStructure {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Require the broken swing point to be an HH (bullish) or an LL (bearish)
  .. Collaborators ..
}

class ChangeOfCharacter {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Require the broken swing point to be an LH (bullish) or an HL (bearish)
  .. Collaborators ..
}

class TimeframeAnalysis {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Know its currency pair and timeframe
  Know its trend: uptrend, downtrend, or ranging
  Know its most recent structure event, if any,
  on its own currency pair and timeframe
  Know its vote (bullish, bearish, or neutral) from its trend
  and its most recent structure event (see Voting)
  .. Collaborators ..
  CurrencyPair
  Timeframe
  StructureEvent
}

class Signal {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Know its M1, M5, H1, and H4 analyses, all for the same currency pair
  Know its direction: the majority of the bullish and bearish votes,
  or no direction on a tie
  Know its score: the number of timeframes voting its direction
  (0 when it has no direction)
  Know its minimum confluence score, a whole number from 1 to 4 (default 3)
  Know whether it is valid: it has a direction and its score
  is at least the minimum (FR8)
  Know its trade direction (bullish leads to buy, bearish leads to sell)
  .. Collaborators ..
  TimeframeAnalysis
}

class TradePlan {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Know the valid signal it is based on
  Own a trade setup with its entry, stop loss, and take profit (TP1),
  in the signal's trade direction
  Know its TP2, beyond TP1
  Reject a reward-to-risk ratio (to TP1) below 2,
  rounded to 2 decimals before comparing (FR2)
  Know its lot size, its risk amount, and its reference timeframe
  Require its risk amount not to exceed the account's
  risk percent of its balance (FR9)
  .. Collaborators ..
  Signal
  TradeSetup
  Timeframe
  Account
}

class Account {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Know its account ID, balance, and currency
  Know its environment and reject any environment other than practice (FR5)
  Know its risk percent, greater than 0 and at most 2 (FR9)
  Know its maximum risk amount per trade
  .. Collaborators ..
}

class Order {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Know the trade plan it was created from
  Know the account it is for, which must be its trade plan's account
  and a practice account (FR10)
  Know that its type is market
  Require the trader's explicit confirmation (FR10)
  Know its units: lot size × 100,000, positive for a buy
  and negative for a sell
  .. Collaborators ..
  TradePlan
  Account
}

class Trade {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Know the order that opened it
  Know its outcome: win, loss, or open (FR11), where a win has
  an R multiple above 0 and a loss an R multiple below 0
  Know its exit price once closed
  Know its R multiple (FR11): the price move from entry to exit
  in its trade direction, divided by its setup's risk; none while open
  .. Collaborators ..
  Order
}
@enduml
